  "notes": [
    "Turnout and votes come from Table 1 (by commune); each constituency's row is its 'Yhteensä - Summa - Total' row, which includes Finnish citizens not in the domicile register in Finland (voters abroad, registered on the constituency electoral roll and able to vote only in advance voting). The national row likewise includes 316305 such registered voters and 6010 such voters. Turnout is on the odd page, party votes on the facing even page.",
    "Table 1 prints no grand-total ballots column: cast = valid + rejected, which equals the printed total voters in every row.",
    "Polling days 15-16 January 1978. Ballots by party are columns of Table 1; the volume has no French text, so 'fr' is null.",
    "Column headers name parties, not candidates, so 'supports' is null. Per the introduction, SDP, KESK, SKDL, KOK, RKP, LKP, STP, SYP and Åländsk samling backed the re-election of Urho Kekkonen; SKL nominated Raino Westerholm, SMP Veikko Vennamo, PKP Ahti Salonen and SKYP Eino Haikala.",
    "Party keys: ml = Keskustapuolue (KESK); pkp = Perustuslaillinen Kansanpuolue; skyp = Suomen Kansan Yhtenäisyyden Puolue; stp = Sosialistinen Työväenpuolue; syp = Suomen Yksityisyrittäjäin Puoluejärjestö; alandsk_samling = Åländsk samling r.f. (Åland coalition list, printed only under its Swedish name).",
    "Electoral alliances (introduction): KESK, LKP and RKP in Helsinki, Uusimaa, Turku South, Kymi and Vaasa; KESK and LKP in Turku North, Häme South and North, Mikkeli, North Karelia, Kuopio, Central Finland and Lapland; SKDL and STP in Turku South, Häme North, Kymi, Mikkeli and North Karelia.",
    "Changes in seat allocation since 1968: Helsinki 32->31, Uusimaa 28->39, Turku South 24->25, Häme South 22->23, Häme North 18->19, Kymi 23->22, Mikkeli 15->13, Kuopio 18->16, North Karelia 13->11, Vaasa 29->27, Central Finland 16->15, Oulu 27->26, Lapland 14->12; Turku North (20) and Åland (1) unchanged. First election of electors with voting age 18 and with advance voting."
  ],
